        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="to-responsibilities">2. Tournament Organizer Responsibilities</h3>
        <p>The Tournament Organizer is responsible for running the event, managing pairings in Longshanks, resolving disputes, and submitting results to the circuit within 14 days. TOs are the final authority at their event on all operational matters.</p>
        <p>If the TO is playing in the event, they must designate a specific non-playing person as the event judge before Round 1 begins. Players must be informed of who to call for rulings.</p>

        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="longshanks">3. Longshanks Configuration</h3>
        <p>All sanctioned events must use Longshanks for pairings, seeding, and result tracking.</p>

        <h4 class="rules-h4">3.1 Event Naming</h4>
        <div class="rules-table-wrap">
          <table class="rules-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Event Type</th><th>Longshanks Name Format</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Shards Event</td><td>Infinity Circuit Shards Event — [Store Name or City]</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Infinity Qualifier</td><td>Infinity Qualifier — [Store Name or City]</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Championship</td><td>Infinity Gauntlet Championship [Year]</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h4 class="rules-h4">3.2 Required Tiebreaker Settings</h4>
        <div class="rules-table-wrap">
          <table class="rules-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Shards Events & Qualifiers</th><th>Championship</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>1st Tiebreaker</td><td>SOS — Average opponent TP</td><td>TOP (Top Table)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>2nd Tiebreaker</td><td>VPS — Victory Points Scored</td><td>SOS — Average opponent TP</td></tr>
              <tr><td>3rd Tiebreaker</td><td>DEN — Direct Encounter</td><td>VPS — Victory Points Scored</td></tr>
              <tr><td>4th Tiebreaker</td><td>—</td><td>DEN — Direct Encounter</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="format">5. Event Format & Pairings</h3>
        <p>All sanctioned events use Swiss pairings under Standard Timeline Marvel: Crisis Protocol rules. There are no progression cuts at Shards Events or Infinity Qualifiers.</p>

        <div class="rules-table-wrap">
          <table class="rules-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Number of Players</th><th>Swiss Rounds</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>5 – 8</td><td>3</td></tr>
              <tr><td>9 – 16</td><td>4</td></tr>
              <tr><td>17 – 32</td><td>5</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="chess-clocks">8. Chess Clocks & Round Timing</h3>
        <p>Chess clocks are the standard timing method for all sanctioned Infinity Circuit events.</p>

        <div class="rules-table-wrap">
          <table class="rules-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Clock per player</td><td>45 minutes</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Overall round timer</td><td>1 hour 45 minutes</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Setup period</td><td>10 minutes (clocks paused)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Clock start</td><td>After deployment and first Power Phase; priority player starts their clock</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Defense rolls</td><td>Made on the attacker's clock</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Clock expiry</td><td>Game ends immediately; player whose clock expired loses</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h4 class="rules-h4">8.2 Round Timer Fallback (No Chess Clocks)</h4>
        <p>If chess clocks are not available, each round uses a 90-minute round timer. When time is called, players have 10 minutes to finish the current game round. At Dice Down, the player with more VPs wins. If VPs are tied, the game is a draw.</p>

        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="components">6. Components & Equipment</h3>
        <p>Players must supply all materials required for play. Key rulings for community events:</p>
        <ul class="rules-list">
          <li>Alternate/3D-printed sculpts (e.g., a different costume version of the same character) are permitted with opponent consent. If the opponent prefers the official model, the player must use it.</li>
          <li>Proxied or printed cards are permitted provided they are accurate reproductions of the current official card and are legible.</li>
          <li>Third-party or custom dice may be used only with the explicit consent of the opponent before the game begins.</li>
          <li>Alternate sculpts are permitted with opponent consent. Proxying one character as a different character is not permitted.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="rules-h3" id="conduct">7. Conduct & Sportsmanship</h3>
        <p>The Infinity Circuit exists to celebrate competitive Marvel: Crisis Protocol and to build a healthy, welcoming regional community. All participants are expected to treat opponents, event staff, and spectators with respect at all times.</p>
        <p>Unsportsmanlike conduct includes disrespectful language or behavior, intentional deception of opponents or judges, deliberate disruption of game components, and slow play for competitive advantage. Consequences range from a warning to disqualification.</p>

        <p class="rules-note">This page summarizes the key rules from both documents. The full PDFs are the authoritative source. In any conflict between this page and the PDFs, the PDFs govern.</p>

